<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-cardamine-hirsuta-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength on Cardamine hirsuta at 154 µm (Pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 88.2/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the same Schnakenberg point (a=0.10, b=0.90, D_u=0.04, D_v=0.42, lambda_c=154.1 µm, age 0 Ma, chronoseries 1/1). Measured record: dispersion Pearson r = 0.999896, RMSE = 0.001564, nonlinear spacing 173.362 µm on both seeds, ablation sigma_max = -0.1016 with the control standard deviation falling, sweep wavelengths 163.9, 173.6, 188.0, 201.0, 217.4 µm (monotonic), specimen foreground fraction 0.2825, bounding-box aspect 0.6048, contour circularity 0.0926, orientation KS 0.0156, radial-FFT Pearson r = 0.9948, GIF 12 frames at 720x540, CV similarity 96.0. The 12% nonlinear shift versus 154.1 µm stays in the record. Overall 88.2/100 (faithfulness 87.6, reproducibility 89.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/cardamine_hirsuta_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-cardamine-hirsuta-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 344427 B, 1440×860 px, artifact_sha256 42f28ae17a71284a0b1d2844190e61edcef85400790a837f1209e520802e70ec (sha256 42f28ae17a71284a0b1d2844190e61edcef85400790a837f1209e520802e70ec), spec_fingerprint 619c6e2e8c89814d4927f6c66381065778340adfaf1d52680367bc6b98ea29d7. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 619c6e2e8c89814d4927f6c66381065778340adfaf1d52680367bc6b98ea29d7; artifact_sha256: 42f28ae17a71284a0b1d2844190e61edcef85400790a837f1209e520802e70ec; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/cardamine_hirsuta_turing_wavelength_s0/README.md=03de545ad27ccbf4..., datasets/cardamine_hirsuta_turing_wavelength_s0/cardamine_hirsuta_specimen.jpg=1c268fecb3660b31..., datasets/cardamine_hirsuta_turing_wavelength_s0/cardamine_hirsuta_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=c696a1319c853366..., datasets/cardamine_hirsuta_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=bfcb6bdfc46bcf19..., datasets/cardamine_hirsuta_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=79d1ae5d5b27c95e...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-cardamine-hirsuta-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) selects a finite critical wavenumber from reaction and diffusion. | Schnakenberg (1979) supplies the kinetics a - u + u^2 v and b - u^2 v. | Hay and Tsiantis (2006), Vlad et al. (2014), and Kierzkowski et al. (2019) establish Cardamine hirsuta as the compound-leaf comparison and tie RCO to domain size rather than to a local wavenumber.; reconstructed_in_script: Neumann Schnakenberg integration, dispersion fit, D_v sweep, and equal-diffusion ablation, now scored from the measurement sidecar. | Specimen mask morphometrics and the orientation KS / radial-FFT comparison against the Commons photograph.; transfer_boundary: 154.1 µm is the classical wavelength of this parameter point, pinned to the slot scale. It is not a length reported by the cited Cardamine papers.; does_not_claim: That the herbarium photograph resolves individual 154 µm ocelli. | A predecessor or successor chronospecies. The series length is 1 and the age is 0 Ma. | That matching the plant's silhouette validates the wavenumber. The wavenumber is tested by the dispersion fit and the spacing measurement.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [independent_assessor/specimen-match, pressure P=0.5]: A second assessor has not scored this loop.",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'D_v sweep monotonicity is now an asserted self-test and a measurement row.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Equal-diffusion ablation sigma_max = -0.1016 is scored, and the flat field is in the comparison figure.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Specimen foreground fraction, aspect, circularity, and coherency are measurement rows with priors that differ from the measured values.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Pearson r = 0.999896, RMSE = 0.001564, and the orientation KS statistic are measurement rows.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Independent second assessor is still absent. Pass 2 remains a single-agent score.', 'status': 'open'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.82e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-cardamine-hirsuta-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength on Cardamine hirsuta at 154 µm (Pass 2) — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
